  "prompt": "I have 5 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) SETTLE OVERDUE BILLS: From settlement worklist `settlements_wl2`, pay each overdue bill that is NOT disputed (skip any invoice with disputed on its dereferenced record — the worklist also lists disputed, archived look-alikes). For each real one, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then its biller to a payout account for the destination IBAN, and pay that exact amount. Then, from worklist `update_email_wl1`, update the account holder's email on file: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (B) CORRECT STANDING ORDERS: From standing-order worklist `standing_orders_wl2`, correct each active standing order that has NOT been superseded (skip superseded on its dereferenced record — the list mixes superseded look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then update the standing order's amount to match it exactly. Then, from worklist `update_payee_wl1`, correct the payee's account details: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (C) AUTOMATE NEW BILLS: From automation worklist `automation_queue_wl2`, automate each bill still awaiting automation that is NOT superseded (skip superseded on its dereferenced record). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then set up a recurring standing order for that exact amount. Then, from worklist `cancel_scheduled_transaction_wl1`, cancel the superseded standing order: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (D) ONBOARD NEW VENDORS: From onboarding worklist `onboarding_queue_wl2`, onboard each APPROVED vendor that is NOT rejected (skip rejected on its dereferenced record). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then add it to the payee registry under its assigned payee id. Then, from worklist `set_daily_limit_wl1`, set the corporate card's daily limit: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (E) REFUND OVERPAYMENTS: From refund worklist `refund_queue_wl2`, refund each overpayment NOT already refunded (skip refunded on its dereferenced record). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then send that same amount back. Then, from worklist `remove_payee_wl1`, remove the delisted payee: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). None of these 5 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier.",
